WP5 red-first evidence
======================

Command:
  PYTHONPATH="$PWD" /home/asa/devel/libresolid-studio/.venv/bin/python \
    -m pytest -q tests/test_flexible_cache_performance.py

Executed before the WP5 production patch, at planning HEAD plus only the new
red tests.  Result: 5 failed.

- The 80-read, three-binding workload constructed 80 meshes instead of 3.
- A forced source/structural `uniq_id` collision served the first mesh to the
  second definition.
- A forced shortened binding-hash collision served the first mesh.
- A serialized-spec change at the same binding was incorrectly a hit.
- The legacy single-binding cache retained 1 entry after four bindings,
  rather than the injected bounded working set of 3.

The failures were the intended existing implementation behavior:
`_flexible_manifold_cache` was keyed by `(uniq_id, binding_hash)` and removed
every entry for that `uniq_id` on each miss.
